{"id": "EUVD-2026-81158", "enisaUuid": "1df76f61-6129-34f3-a4a8-9cc9291ed969", "description": "A vulnerability in the SSID bring-your-own-device (BYOD) onboarding workflow of Cisco ISE could allow an unauthenticated, adjacent attacker to hijack the onboarding session of&nbsp;another user and access protected 802.1X networks. &nbsp;\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to insufficient authentication checks that are performed while a user is being onboarded. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by spoofing the legitimate user and triggering&nbsp;a redirection to the guest web portal. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to take over the user session and gain access to the protected 802.1X network.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T20:20:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-17T14:05:45", "baseScore": 3.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:N/I:L/A:N", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-ise-multi-vuln-kWLeNnRD"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-20071", "GHSA-mc6q-xfc2-72q5"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00e3789e-09d5-3958-ba1f-bc4d9b7caf96", "product": {"name": "Cisco Identity Services Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.2 Patch 8"}, {"id": "0c8d347e-1b3d-3f6e-b8c0-f4ae2ef8ab57", "product": {"name": "Cisco Identity Services Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.3 Patch 12"}, {"id": "11976688-57df-3223-a502-4450bf16afb5", "product": {"name": "Cisco Identity Services Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.5 Patch 1"}, {"id": "12bc0f7d-822e-31ef-a18b-2d57ed0f2669", "product": {"name": "Cisco Identity Services Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.3 Patch 1"}, {"id": "167c4c0c-d51d-3df6-abb4-db5c1fb336d6", "product": {"name": "Cisco Identity Services Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_ve